course: dictionary
lesson: 9834
title: Swiftly: quick, and soon
level: primary-5
stars: 2
explain: Swiftly is an adverb, a word that tells you how something is done. Its main meaning is quickly or fast. Stories often use it instead of «quickly», so it is good to know it when you read.
explain: Swiftly can also mean very soon, without any delay. A safety rule might say «leave the building swiftly and calmly», which means get out fast, but do not panic. The words around swiftly give you the clues: calmly tells you it is about moving sensibly, not running wildly.
explain: In «The voice died away and ceased as an insect's tiny trumpet dwindles swiftly into silence», the word swiftly tells you how quickly the sound fades. Ask yourself: what word would fit here? Quickly fits, so swiftly means quickly in this sentence.
fact: Swiftly means quickly or fast.
fact: Swiftly can also mean happening very soon, without delay.
fact: Swiftly is an adverb, so it often tells you how an action happens.
fact: «Dwindles swiftly into silence» means the sound fades away quickly.
fact: Numbers in maths stories tell you the actual speed, even if a sentence says swiftly.
exercise: In «an insect's tiny trumpet dwindles swiftly into silence», what does swiftly mean? | Loudly | *Quickly, fast | Slowly and carefully | Happily
exercise: In a safety rule, «leave the building swiftly and calmly», what should you do? | *Get out quickly, without delay, and stay calm | Take a long time to pack your bag | Stop and sit down | Walk slowly to look around
exercise: Which word is closest in meaning to swiftly? | Sleepily | Heavily | Slowly | *Speedily
test: The teacher asked the class to answer swiftly. What does this ask them to do? | *Answer without delay | Wait for a long time | Write a story first | Shout the answer
test: The nurse said the doctor would come swiftly. What does swiftly suggest? | *Coming very soon, without delay | Never coming | Coming after lunch next week | Coming on a bicycle
exam: In «dwindles swiftly into silence», which word could replace swiftly? | *Quickly | Loudly | Gently | Happily
